        <p>
          This privacy policy applies to optional OpenCam update emails and to the OpenCam app (hereby referred to as "Application") for iOS that was created by QI ZHI (hereby referred to as "Service Provider") as a Freemium service. This service is intended for use "AS IS".
        </p>
        
        <h3>What information does the Application obtain and how is it used?</h3>
        <p>
          OpenCam’s camera functionality processes your recordings on your device. Registration and an email subscription are not required to use the Application. The optional email-update service described below is separate from camera functionality.
        </p>

        <h3>Does the Application collect precise real time location information of the device?</h3>
        <p>
          This Application does not collect any information about the location of your iPhone.
        </p>

        <h3>Do third parties see and/or have access to information obtained by the Application?</h3>
        <p>
          Camera recordings are not sent to the email-update service. If you choose to sign up for update emails, the service providers described below process the information needed to run that service.
        </p>

        <h3>What are my opt-out rights?</h3>
        <p>
            You can unsubscribe from update emails using the link in each announcement without an account. Uninstalling the Application does not unsubscribe you. To request deletion of your email-service data, contact hello@opencam.app.
        </p>

        <h3>Optional update emails</h3>
        <p>If you sign up, we collect your email address, signup source (such as the website or app), signup and consent times (and confirmation times where applicable), and the version of the consent wording you accepted. We use these records to send OpenCam news, features, announcements, and releases and manage your subscription. We do not sell your email address or use this list for unrelated marketing.</p>
        <p>Submitting the signup form subscribes you immediately; no confirmation email is sent. Cloudflare Workers and D1 process and store subscription records, and Cloudflare Turnstile checks signup requests for abuse invisibly in the background, as described in the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/" class="underline">Cloudflare Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a>. Resend sends emails and processes delivery, bounce, and complaint events. These providers may process data in countries outside your country of residence. We do not use tracking pixels in update emails.</p>
        <p>While the existing Google Form remains linked, Google processes submissions to that form. Existing form signups may be migrated with their original consent evidence; joining TestFlight alone does not subscribe you to update emails.</p>
        <p>We keep active subscription and consent records while you remain subscribed. Unconfirmed new signups are removed after 30 days. Short-lived hashed rate-limit records expire within a day. Delivery history and minimal unsubscribe or suppression records are retained to investigate delivery problems and prevent unwanted future email; you can request deletion at hello@opencam.app. Backups may retain deleted records until their normal expiry. Unsubscribing stops future queued announcements, though an email already handed to the delivery provider may still arrive.</p>

        <h3>Children</h3>
        <p>
          The Application is not used to knowingly solicit data from or market to children under the age of 13.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Service Provider does not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children. The Service Provider encourages all children to never submit any personally identifiable information through the Application and/or Services. The Service Provider encourage parents and legal guardians to monitor their children's Internet usage and to help enforce this Policy by instructing their children never to provide personally identifiable information through the Application and/or Services without their permission. If you have reason to believe that a child has provided personally identifiable information to the Service Provider through the Application and/or Services, please contact the Service Provider (hello@opencam.app) so that they will be able to take the necessary actions. You must also be at least 16 years of age to consent to the processing of your personally identifiable information in your country (in some countries we may allow your parent or guardian to do so on your behalf).
        </p>

        <h3>Security</h3>
        <p>
          We restrict access to email-service records and protect confirmation and unsubscribe tokens. No online service can guarantee absolute security.
        </p>

        <h3>Changes</h3>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time for any reason. The Service Provider will notify you of any changes to their Privacy Policy by updating this page with the new Privacy Policy. You are advised to consult this Privacy Policy regularly for any changes, as continued use is deemed approval of all changes.
        </p>

        <h3>Your Consent</h3>
        <p>
          Email-update consent is optional and is given by submitting the signup form. You can withdraw that consent at any time by unsubscribing.
        </p>

        <h3>Contact Us</h3>
        <p>
          If you have any questions regarding privacy while using the Application, or have questions about the practices, please contact the Service Provider via email at hello@opencam.app.
